  "notes": "Commit = tag 2.19.3 (the 2.19 line of the advisory; the benchmark's 3.x source needs Java 21 at run time, the fixture runs on Java 17). Gradle projects :server and :libs:opensearch-{cli,common,compress,core,geo,secure-sm,task-commons,telemetry,x-content}; only the jar tasks, tests not run. The init script (written into the work directory, outside the source tree) disables the Spotless formatting check: gradle/formatting.gradle points the Spotless Eclipse formatter to a P2 mirror that no longer serves eclipse/updates/4.29 and buildSrc realizes every task at configuration time, so configuration would fail ('Failed to load eclipse jdt formatter'); no Spotless task runs. org.gradle.jvmargs = the project's gradle.properties with -Xmx6g; --max-workers is a resource flag. Version: build.snapshot defaults to true, so the jars are 2.19.3-SNAPSHOT; every entry equals the Central 2.19.3 jars' except META-INF/MANIFEST.MF. The original recipe also generated the POMs (generatePomFileForNebulaPublication) to check the fixture's third-party declarations; that step is not needed for the jars. Fixed: the ten artifacts at 2.19.4 (PR #19491 backport); 2.19.4 also bumps Lucene to 9.12.3, which drop does not replace (the fixture keeps its Lucene 9.12.2)."
